A||N||19||Eric_PA||Fire Fire Fire :(||||8||
Z||000000||Eric_PA||09-22-2001||12:20 AM||||Tonight I almost lost my Fiero driving down interstate 78. I was working on the car earlier today so I could drive it to the Reading show this weekend. It had a bad coolant line for the transmission, and I decided to fix it. I was hesitant on making the repair since I plan on taking the whole power plant out in a week or two to install the 3800 with a 5 speed. I wish I would have let it alone in the drive way until I was ready to do the swap. The way this happened was, I left my place to take it on a test drive and decided to merge on to a local highway (I-78) about a mile from the on ramp, I smelled something burning. I looked in my rearview and couldn't see a thing but black smoke. I quickly pulled over to the side and shut off the car, popped the decklid. As soon as I got out I saw flames under the drivers side vent above the air cleaner. The trans fluid was again leaking and had spayed all over the cat and caught fire on the fire wall. I didn't know what to do, no one was pulling over to offer help and I thought the car was going to burn to the ground.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I decide to get away from the car and try to waive someone down. 5 minutes later an off duty officer stopped and called the fire company/state police. They were there in under 5 minutes. They responded quickly. The good news is...... would you belive the fire went out on its own... I feel so darn lucky. I guess it didn't burn since I had stripped all of the insulation in the engine compartment. I think that if it where still in there the car would have burned to the ground. The reason why I think this is because it would have soaked up all of the tranny fluid and acted like a wick. I towed the car home and it now sets ready for my 3800. Keep in mind that this car didn't catch on fire because it was a Fiero, it was because of my stupidity to rig up a cooling line that wasn't rated for the pressure from the tranny. <P>Lesson learned.... I will keep a fire extinguisher with me for now on. ||||reg||8
Z||000001||FieroHeather||09-22-2001||12:23 AM||||Im glad to hear that you got her home safely, and that you were not hurt in the process!||||reg||4
Z||000002||Kwez||09-22-2001||12:24 AM||||sorry for your misfortune ...<BR>but glad for the outcome.<P>will I ever get my a$$ moving & buy a fire extinguisher !?<P>good luck w. the 3800 swap  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||13
Z||000003||MinnGreenGT||09-22-2001||12:28 AM||||Maybe you and AUS should hang out... you know- have a Bar-B-Q or something.  J/K- <P>my condolences... glad to hear that the car survived farily well.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000004||Posthumane||09-22-2001||12:28 AM||||You should get a small fire extinguisher and put it on top of the center console like I did, so it's visible for all to see out the back window. It's my symbol for fiero pride  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. Some guys in the calgary fiero club were saying I'm making them all look bad by displaying that extinguisher like a badge. Anyway, good to hear there was no major damage.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Brandon86SE||09-22-2001||12:50 AM||||post - hehehe, I remember saying that!  I was the only guy there when you showed up for your first meeting.  I guess I missed ya Thursday, I was there, but working and only there for a bit while I was on break.<P>Eric - great to hear you (and your car) are relatively fine.  Any chance the cop/ firemen give you a hard time about having a Fiero on fire on the side of the freeway?<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Hank is Here||09-22-2001||12:50 AM||||I thought of this today.  I cary an abc extinguisher with me.  It sits at the bottom on my trunk so it can be hard to ge to.  I need to find a place to mount it.  Every vehicle that I own that is drivable has its own extinguisher.  I refuse to loose a car to flames.  <P>This is a simple task to do.  My extinguisher was under $10 at wally-world, worth it for the piece of mind.   ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Posthumane||09-22-2001||12:58 AM||||Brandon, I couldn't make it thursday. As I was pulling out of the driveway from my mom's house to go to willy's, my clutch finally kicked the bucket. Today I took the master cylinder apart and found the spring inside it had broke, so it wouldn't open up the valve to pull fluid from the reservoir, and i couldn't disengage the clutch. I also have to flush out the whole system cuz the fluid in it is completely opaque, and almost black. Should be at the next one tho.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Brandon86SE||09-22-2001||03:04 AM||||Ouch, that's too bad.  I had to get my clutch done a year ago.  I wish I was a little more willing to do stuff myself then, as I got charged $900 to get it done at the shop!!  They told me they had to take the engine out to get at the clutch......?  Anyway, best of luck to ya.  I guess you probably won't be ready for the Red Deer run next Sunday, eh?  They're a riot!  If at all possible, try to make it.  Cya,<P>Brandon||||reg||13
Z||000009||JayUSA77||09-22-2001||12:53 PM||||hey guys i was just looking at <A HREF="http://www.homedepot.com" TARGET=_blank>www.homedepot.com</A>  and i found a fire extinguisher for about 36 bucks brand new. heres the pic<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fire_1.jpg"> <BR>the best thing about it is you can order them from over the internet right to your front door.<BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||rogergarrison||09-22-2001||01:04 PM||||I always carry an extinquisher as should you all. One big tip, DONT STORE IT IN THE REAR COMPARTMENT, YOU WONT BE ABLE TO GET IT WHEN YOU NEED IT. Keep it in the front or passenger compartment.||||reg||1
Z||000011||dennis_6||09-22-2001||07:27 PM||||Summit and Jegs both sell a remote fire extinquisher.  You could put it in the front hood and have it spray into the passenger compartment and engine compartment at the same time.  The spray is clear and the residue is clear so it won't block your vision.  The system does cost around 300 bucks though.||||reg||10
Z||000012||fierospeeder||09-23-2001||01:50 AM||||You have to go to nappa, where they can cut you lines in whatever size you like.<P><BR>Transmission line is a special rubber hose with small threads(string) in the rubber, and they dont break down to exposure of oil.  You have to do the same when you buy powersteering return line hose.  ||||reg||1
Z||000013||FieroLisa||09-23-2001||06:42 PM||||Yah I had a seal go on my brake line, spewing break fluid all over the rear driver side rim- had to drive 300 miles like that, I was scared to death it would catch fire if I hit my brakes and they got hot... so I put my little fire extinguisher in my passenger seat and downshifted to stop  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Yay for my grand am upgrade this weekend, took care of that problem!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">     <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>AIM: FieroLisa||||reg||1
